01:06:18,947 --> 01:06:24,947
Nickel Boys is a 2024 American historical drama film based on the
2019 novel The Nickel Boys by Colson Whitehead.

10
01:13:41,052 --> 01:13:47,052
It was directed by RaMell Ross, who wrote the screenplay with Joslyn Barnes.

11
01:21:03,157 --> 01:21:09,157
Starring Ethan Herisse, Brandon Wilson, Hamish Linklater, Fred Hechinger, Daveed Diggs, Jimmie Fails, and Aunjanue Ellis-Taylor, the story
follows two African-American boys, Elwood (Herisse) and Turner (Wilson), who are sent to an abusive reform school in 1960s Florida.

12
01:28:25,263 --> 01:28:31,263
The film is inspired by the Dozier School for Boys, a now-closed Florida
reform school notorious for its abusive treatment of students.

13
01:35:47,368 --> 01:35:53,368
The film was shot from a first-person point-of-view, with
filming taking place in Louisiana in late 2022.

14
01:43:09,473 --> 01:43:15,473
It premiered at the 51st Telluride Film Festival on August 30, 2024, and had a
limited theatrical release by Amazon MGM Studios on December 13, 2024.

15
01:50:31,578 --> 01:50:37,578
It was named one of the top 10 films of 2024 by the American Film Institute and received numerous accolades, including the award for Best Cinematography at the 40th Independent Spirit
Awards, a Best Motion Picture – Drama nomination at the 82nd Golden Globe Awards and two nominations at the 97th Academy Awards for Best Picture and Best Adapted Screenplay.

16
01:57:53,684 --> 01:57:59,684
IndieWire named it the best film of the 2020s, as of 2025, and it has
been cited by others as among the best of the 21st century.

17
02:05:15,789 --> 02:05:21,789
The film explores themes of florida, new york city, sexual
abuse, based on novel or book, alligator.

